From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:34:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: pmp: keep T8132's __DATA across a deep
 sleep

The wake program reloads the PMP's __TEXT from DRAM, and nothing restores
__DATA. Back up the second of the ADT's segment-ranges.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit d8d705bbb245e38c00de45aad69a637c2ef74e16)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs
index ff2c1bf973..337be41924 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs
@@ -890,11 +890,13 @@ enum Ep7 {
     sram_backup: None,
 };
 
+/// T8132: the sleep engine reloads `__TEXT` from DRAM at the wake, and only `__DATA`
+/// (the ADT's second segment) has to be kept.
 const HW_CFG_T8132: PmpHwConfig = PmpHwConfig {
     dma_mask: None,
     check_bootargs_uuid: false,
     coreanalytics: Ep7::RetainedBoard,
-    sram_backup: None,
+    sram_backup: Some((0x3c000, 0x68000)),
 };
 
 impl Drop for PmpDriver {
-- 
2.43.0

